   "reasoning_summary": "C12H22O11 with DoU 2 and all 1H signals at 3.5-4.6 ppm in D2O points to a disaccharide with 14 CH protons and 8 OH exchanged. Twenty-two 13C signals, with no C=O and no signal near 92-96 ppm, indicate a ketose-containing reducing disaccharide present as an equilibrium of tautomers. Ketal and anomeric carbons appear at 105.6, 103.5 and 100.8 ppm. Furanose ring carbons appear at 86.9, 82.8 and 80.1 ppm. The anomeric protons at 4.56 and 4.46 ppm (ids 1, 2) are typical of beta-galactoside H1 in two fructose tautomers. Lactulose is therefore favored over alpha-linked palatinose or turanose. Shifts appear offset by about 1-2 ppm, depending on referencing. Peak 2 is treated as the minor-tautomer H1, so it is given 0 protons in the 14-proton count."
  },
